# What must never reach a wordpress.org download.
#
# ⚠️ EVERY ONE OF THESE WAS IN THE PLUGIN WHEN PLUGIN CHECK WAS FIRST RUN AGAINST IT,
# and between them they produced 41 of the 44 findings — including the only two errors.
#
#   bin/            developer CLI scripts. Plugin Check reads them as plugin code.
#   .gitignore      "Hidden files are not permitted."
#   README.md,
#   SUBMISSION.md   "Unexpected markdown file in plugin root." readme.txt is the one
#                   wordpress.org renders; README.md is for somebody reading the source.
#   assets/         the listing artwork. wordpress.org serves it from the SVN assets/
#                   directory, not from the plugin — shipping it would put PNGs on every
#                   install to draw a page nobody sees from inside their dashboard.
.git
.gitignore
.distignore
bin
README.md
SUBMISSION.md
assets
